invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select broadcasts the mask it computed and not the value it
  reads back through its volatile pointer, so the compiler sees which
  entry each mask keeps and may branch on the digit, as clang for x86-64
  did for rsa_sign64.c's read. The bytes stay right.
  inv-16-rsa-ifma-table-read refuses a broadcast in table_select of any
  value but the one read back.

--- old
            rsa_ifma_lanes mask = lanes_broadcast(*hidden);
--- new
            rsa_ifma_lanes mask = lanes_broadcast(mask_of_bit(differ ^ 1));
